B.aet=new A.bC("heart-after-menopause",B.eU,"Does menopause affect my heart?",B.biU,B.b8J,B.bgI,"Ask your doctor to check your heart risk, including blood pressure, cholesterol and blood sugar.",B.aWU,B.b63)
B.brl=s(["My LDL is high","What foods lower cholesterol?","Cholesterol went up after menopause"],t.s)
B.b2A=s(["cholesterol","ldl","hdl","lipids","triglycerides","statin"],t.s)
B.bjh=s(["Cholesterol often rises after menopause. Food can make a real difference, especially:","\u2022 Soluble fibre: oats, barley, beans, lentils, apples, psyllium.\n\u2022 Nuts, about a handful a day.\n\u2022 Soy foods, like tofu, edamame and soy drinks.\n\u2022 Swapping saturated fats (fatty meats, butter, cream, coconut oil) for olive or canola oil, avocado, nuts and seeds.\n\u2022 Foods with added plant sterols.",'Together these make up the "Portfolio diet", developed in Canada. Being active and keeping alcohol low help too.'],t.s)
B.b7M=s([B.Xu,B.ro,B.rq],t.P)
B.bR8=new A.f0(null,"hdl",13,"hdl")
B.aYN=s([B.a_O,B.bR8,B.a_J,B.na],t.G)
B.aeO=new A.bC("cholesterol",B.eU,"How can I lower my cholesterol with food?",B.brl,B.b2A,B.bjh,"Your doctor looks at cholesterol together with your other risks to decide whether you need medicine. Food changes still help either way.",B.b7M,B.aYN)
B.b8A=s(["High blood pressure","Does salt raise blood pressure?","Hypertension"],t.s)
B.bkN=s(["pressure","hypertension","salt","sodium"],t.s)
B.b3U=s(["Blood pressure tends to rise after menopause, often without any symptoms, so checking it regularly matters.","Helpful habits: less sodium (most comes from packaged and restaurant food, not the salt shaker), more vegetables, fruit and potassium-rich foods, regular activity, less alcohol, and managing stress. Health Canada suggests adults stay under 2,300 mg of sodium a day."],t.s)
B.boY=s([B.XL,B.Xm],t.P)
B.bR5=new A.f0(B.r8,null,11,"potassium")
B.bnN=s([B.a_K,B.bR5],t.G)
B.aeZ=new A.bC("blood-pressure",B.eU,"How can I keep my blood pressure healthy?",B.b8A,B.bkN,B.b3U,"Have your blood pressure checked at least once a year, or as your doctor suggests.",B.boY,B.bnN)
B.b3M=s(["My blood sugar is high","What is A1C?","Diabetes risk"],t.s)
B.biz=s(["sugar","glucose","a1c","hba1c","prediabetes","diabetes","insulin"],t.s)
B.b2r=s(["Prediabetes means blood sugar is higher than normal but not high enough to be diabetes. Diabetes Canada describes it as an A1C of 6.0 to 6.4% or a fasting glucose of 6.1 to 6.9 mmol/L.","It is a warning sign, and often reversible. Being active (including strength work), more fibre and whole foods, fewer sugary drinks and refined carbs, and losing a little weight if needed can bring it back down."],t.s)
B.b4K=s([B.Xa,B.z9],t.P)
B.bR7=new A.f0(null,"hba1c",14,"hba1c")
B.bR6=new A.f0(null,"glucose_fasting",15,"glucoseFasting")
B.a_M=new A.f0(B.rc,null,8,"sugar")
B.bqr=s([B.bR7,B.bR6,B.a_M],t.G)
B.aef=new A.bC("blood-sugar",B.eU,"What does prediabetes mean?",B.b3M,B.biz,B.b2r,"Your doctor will tell you how often to recheck. Ask about your diabetes risk if it runs in your family.",B.b4K,B.bqr)
B.aOP=s(["Chest pain","Heart attack symptoms women","Stroke signs"],t.s)
B.b4E=s(["attack","chest","stroke","emergency","fast"],t.s)
B.b3A=s(["Heart attack signs include chest pain or pressure, discomfort in the arms, neck, jaw, shoulders or back, shortness of breath, nausea, sweating and light-headedness. Women more often have the less typical signs, like breathlessness, nausea or back or jaw pain.","For stroke, remember FAST: Face drooping, Arms can't be raised, Speech slurred or jumbled, Time to call 911."],t.s)
B.b5J=s([B.ru,B.mH],t.P)
B.aeM=new A.bC("heart-attack-signs",B.eU,"What are the signs of a heart attack or stroke in women?",B.aOP,B.b4E,B.b3A,"Call 911 right away. Don't drive yourself to hospital.",B.b5J,B.bD)
B.beE=s(["Is my result normal?","My lab result is flagged","Understanding lab results"],t.s)
B.b6l=s(["blood","test","results","lab","range","normal","flagged","bloodwork"],t.s)
B.b5y=s(["Each lab prints its own reference range: the span where most healthy people fall. A result just outside it isn't always a problem, and one inside it isn't always ideal for you. What matters is the whole picture: your history, symptoms and how results change over time.","Blood work in Daisy keeps your results and their trends, and makes a PDF to bring to your appointment."],t.s)
B.b2B=s([B.zp],t.P)
B.ae8=new A.bC("blood-results",B.eU,"What do my blood test results mean?",B.beE,B.b6l,B.b5y,"Your doctor is the right person to explain your results. Write your questions down before the visit.",B.b2B,B.bD)
B.aIS=s(["Thyroid and menopause","What is TSH?","Underactive thyroid"],t.s)
B.bo2=s(["thyroid","tsh","hypothyroid","t4"],t.s)
B.bgW=s(["Thyroid problems are common in women in midlife, and an underactive thyroid shares many signs with menopause: tiredness, weight gain, low mood, feeling cold, dry skin and hair changes.","A simple blood test (TSH) can check it, and treatment is straightforward if it is low."],t.s)
B.b3w=s([B.zd,B.Xy],t.P)
B.b57=s([B.B5],t.G)
B.ae7=new A.bC("thyroid",B.eU,"Could it be my thyroid?",B.aIS,B.bo2,B.bgW,"If you have these symptoms, ask your doctor whether a thyroid test makes sense.",B.b3w,B.b57)
B.bqu=s(["Low ferritin","Iron rich foods","Am I anaemic?","Anemia"],t.s)
B.b2O=s(["iron","ferritin","anaemia","anemia","anaemic","anemic","hemoglobin"],t.s)
B.b7e=s(["Heavy periods in perimenopause can lower iron, which can cause tiredness, breathlessness, pale skin and hair loss. After periods stop, women need less iron (about 8 mg a day instead of 18).","Iron is in meat, fish, poultry, beans, lentils, tofu, fortified cereals and dark greens. Eating plant iron with vitamin C (peppers, citrus, tomatoes) helps you absorb it, and tea or coffee with meals lowers it."],t.s)
B.aR_=s([B.zn,B.XK],t.P)
B.brw=s([B.B3,B.nb,B.B4],t.G)
B.aeD=new A.bC("iron",B.eU,"Do I need more iron?",B.bqu,B.b2O,B.b7e,"Don't take iron supplements without a blood test: too much iron can be harmful. Ask your doctor if you are tired or have heavy periods.",B.aR_,B.brw)
B.b2J=s(["Low B12","B12 after 50"],t.s)
B.b4A=s(["b12","cobalamin","tingling","numbness","pins"],t.s)
B.b5f=s(["Vitamin B12 keeps nerves and blood healthy. As we get older the body absorbs less from food, and some medicines (like metformin and stomach-acid reducers) lower it further.","It is found in meat, fish, eggs, milk and fortified plant drinks and cereals. Vegans and many people over 50 rely on fortified foods or a supplement."],t.s)
B.bcN=s([B.zc],t.P)
B.a_L=new A.f0(B.r9,null,10,"vitaminB12")
B.aRk=s([B.a_L,B.a_N],t.G)
B.ael=new A.bC("b12",B.eU,"Do I need vitamin B12?",B.b2J,B.b4A,B.b5f,"Tiredness, tingling or numbness can be signs of low B12: ask your doctor about a blood test.",B.bcN,B.aRk)
B.bjY=s(["Best diet for menopause","Healthy eating in midlife","Menopause foods","What can I eat to help with symptoms?"],t.s)
B.b2K=s(["diet","eat","eating","nutrition","meals","healthy"],t.s)
B.b9b=s(["There is no special menopause diet, but some things matter more now: protein at each meal for muscle, calcium and vitamin D for bones, fibre and healthy fats for the heart, and lots of colourful vegetables and fruit.","Canada's food guide is a good simple pattern: half your plate vegetables and fruit, a quarter whole grains, a quarter protein foods, with water as your drink of choice.","Limiting alcohol, caffeine and very spicy food can help if they trigger your hot flashes."],t.s)
B.b2m=s([B.k4,B.rp],t.P)
B.bf6=s([B.tx,B.ty,B.na],t.G)
B.aee=new A.bC("menopause-diet",B.em,"What should I eat during menopause?",B.bjY,B.b2K,B.b9b,null,B.b2m,B.bf6)
B.baH=s(["High fiber foods","Am I eating enough fiber?"],t.s)
B.bbp=s(["fibre","fiber","whole","grains","oats","beans"],t.s)
B.b8O=s(["Most Canadians eat only about half the fibre they need. Women are advised to aim for about 21 to 25 g a day.","Fibre helps digestion, keeps you full, and helps cholesterol and blood sugar. Good sources: oats, whole grain bread and pasta, beans, lentils, chickpeas, vegetables, fruit with the skin, nuts and seeds. Add it slowly and drink more water to avoid bloating."],t.s)
B.aOO=s([B.z5,B.Xd],t.P)
B.ae5=new A.bC("fibre",B.em,"How much fibre do I need?",B.baH,B.bbp,B.b8O,null,B.aOO,B.LT)
B.brv=s(["Phytoestrogens","Is soy safe?","Flaxseed for hot flashes"],t.s)
B.b5T=s(["soy","soya","tofu","edamame","phytoestrogens","isoflavones","flax","flaxseed"],t.s)
B.bbo=s(["Soy foods contain plant compounds (isoflavones) that act a little like weak oestrogen. Studies show a small effect on hot flashes for some women, but results are mixed.","Soy foods like tofu, edamame and soy drinks are a healthy protein either way, and are considered safe as part of a normal diet. Supplements with concentrated isoflavones are less well studied."],t.s)
B.b2o=s([B.za,B.k4],t.P)
B.aeF=new A.bC("soy",B.em,"Does soy help with menopause?",B.brv,B.b5T,B.bbo,"If you have had breast cancer, ask your doctor before taking soy supplements.",B.b2o,B.bD)
B.b7s=s(["Fish oil","Fatty fish","Omega 3 foods"],t.s)
B.bc7=s(["omega","omega3","fish","salmon","oil","walnuts","chia"],t.s)
B.b4a=s(["Omega-3 fats are good for the heart and brain. Eating fatty fish like salmon, trout, sardines or mackerel twice a week is a common suggestion.","Plant sources (ground flax, chia, walnuts, canola oil, soy) give a different omega-3 called ALA; women need about 1.1 g a day."],t.s)
B.be7=s([B.ro,B.k4],t.P)
B.bR4=new A.f0(B.r5,null,5,"omega3")
B.bpw=s([B.bR4],t.G)
B.aea=new A.bC("omega-3",B.em,"Do I need omega-3s?",B.b7s,B.bc7,B.b4a,"Check with your doctor or pharmacist before taking fish oil capsules if you take blood thinners.",B.be7,B.bpw)
B.bn0=s(["Does caffeine make hot flashes worse?","Caffeine and sleep"],t.s)
B.b3t=s(["coffee","caffeine","tea","espresso","energy drink"],t.s)
B.bry=s(["Health Canada says most adults can safely have up to 400 mg of caffeine a day, about three 8 oz (237 ml) cups of brewed coffee.","In menopause, caffeine can trigger hot flashes, palpitations and bladder urgency, and it can disturb sleep for many hours. Having it only before noon, or trying half-caf, helps many women."],t.s)
B.biY=s([B.Xe,B.rt],t.P)
B.aeb=new A.bC("caffeine",B.em,"How much coffee is OK?",B.bn0,B.b3t,B.bry,null,B.biY,B.bD)
B.b5e=s(["Is wine bad for me?","Alcohol and menopause","A glass of wine"],t.s)
B.b4Z=s(["alcohol","wine","beer","drink","drinks","drinking","cocktail"],t.s)
B.bqv=s(["Canada's Guidance on Alcohol and Health (2023) says less is better. At two standard drinks or fewer a week you are likely to avoid harms. At three to six, the risk of several cancers (including breast cancer) goes up, and at seven or more the risk of heart disease and stroke rises significantly.","A standard drink is a 142 ml (5 oz) glass of 12% wine, a 341 ml bottle of 5% beer, or 43 ml of 40% spirits. Alcohol can also trigger hot flashes and break up sleep."],t.s)
B.aOL=s([B.Xj,B.rt],t.P)
B.aeG=new A.bC("alcohol",B.em,"How much alcohol is safe?",B.b5e,B.b4Z,B.bqv,null,B.aOL,B.bD)
B.bge=s(["Am I drinking enough?","Hydration"],t.s)
B.bjX=s(["water","hydration","hydrated","thirsty","fluids"],t.s)
B.bfU=s(["There is no single number: needs change with heat, activity and hot flashes. A good guide is drinking regularly through the day so your urine is pale yellow. Food (fruit, vegetables, soups) counts too.","Canada's food guide suggests making water your drink of choice. If bladder leaks or night-time bathroom trips are a problem, drink steadily during the day and a little less in the evening rather than cutting back overall."],t.s)
B.b4r=s([B.rp,B.rv],t.P)
B.aep=new A.bC("water",B.em,"How much water should I drink?",B.bge,B.bjX,B.bfU,null,B.b4r,B.bD)
B.bdK=s(["Sweet cravings","Snacking at night","Always hungry"],t.s)
B.biZ=s(["craving","cravings","sweet","sweets","snack","snacking","hungry","chocolate"],t.s)
B.aIR=s(["Cravings often come from tiredness, stress, long gaps between meals, or meals low in protein and fibre.","Regular meals with protein, fibre and some healthy fat keep blood sugar steadier. Having a planned snack (yogurt and fruit, nuts, hummus and veggies) helps, and so does better sleep. Health Canada suggests limiting added sugars."],t.s)
B.bdN=s([B.z9,B.k4],t.P)
B.boC=s([B.a_M,B.tx,B.na],t.G)
B.aeL=new A.bC("sugar-cravings",B.em,"Why do I crave sugar?",B.bdK,B.biZ,B.aIR,null,B.bdN,B.boC)
B.b65=s(["Which vitamins should I take?","Do I need supplements?"],t.s)
B.b3J=s(["multivitamin","multivitamins","vitamins","supplements"],t.s)
B.aP2=s(["Most nutrients are best from food, and a varied diet covers most of what you need. A few are harder to get from food after 50:","\u2022 Vitamin D: Health Canada recommends a daily 400 IU supplement for everyone over 50.\n\u2022 Vitamin B12: absorbed less well with age; fortified foods or a supplement can help.\n\u2022 Calcium: only if food falls short of about 1,200 mg a day.","A basic multivitamin for adults over 50 is a simple way to cover vitamin D and B12 for some women. More is not better: high doses of some vitamins and minerals can be harmful."],t.s)
B.aR6=s([B.zo,B.zh,B.zc],t.P)
B.b6H=s([B.B2,B.a_L,B.ty],t.G)
B.aeT=new A.bC("multivitamin",B.em,"Should I take a multivitamin?",B.b65,B.b3J,B.aP2,"Ask your doctor or pharmacist before starting supplements, especially if you take medicines.",B.aR6,B.b6H)
B.aky=s(["Magnesium for sleep","Magnesium foods"],t.s)
B.MD=s(["magnesium"],t.s)
B.b7B=s(["Magnesium is needed for muscles, nerves and bones. Women over 30 need about 320 mg a day, which most people can get from nuts, seeds, beans, whole grains, leafy greens and dark chocolate.","Magnesium supplements are popular for sleep and cramps, but the evidence is limited. High doses from supplements can cause diarrhoea."],t.s)
B.b6r=s([B.XM],t.P)
B.bRa=new A.f0(B.r6,null,9,"magnesium")
B.b6g=s([B.bRa],t.G)
B.aeV=new A.bC("magnesium",B.em,"Should I take magnesium?",B.aky,B.MD,B.b7B,"Ask your doctor or pharmacist first, especially if you have kidney problems or take other medicines.",B.b6r,B.b6g)
B.bga=s(["Bladder leaks","Incontinence menopause","I always need to pee","Pelvic floor"],t.s)
B.b6n=s(["leak","leaks","leaking","bladder","incontinence","pee","urine","pelvic","kegel"],t.s)
B.aR0=s(["Bladder leaks and urgency become more common after menopause, as lower oestrogen and weaker pelvic floor muscles affect bladder control. It is common, but not something you just have to live with.","Pelvic floor exercises (Kegels) done daily help a lot, especially for leaks when you cough, laugh or sneeze. The Pelvic floor trainer in Daisy guides you through them. Less caffeine and alcohol helps urgency."],t.s)
B.b3D=s([B.rv,B.XJ,B.Xh],t.P)
B.aeU=new A.bC("bladder-leaks",B.mI,"Why do I leak when I cough or sneeze?",B.bga,B.b6n,B.aR0,"Ask your doctor about it, and about a pelvic floor physiotherapist. Vaginal oestrogen can also help.",B.b3D,B.bD)
B.aks=s(["UTI after menopause","Burning when I pee"],t.s)
B.b3S=s(["uti","utis","infection","infections","burning","cystitis"],t.s)
B.b5U=s(["After menopause, thinner tissue and changes in vaginal bacteria make urinary tract infections more likely.","Drinking enough, not holding urine for long, and peeing after sex help. For repeat infections, vaginal oestrogen has good evidence for lowering how often they happen."],t.s)
B.b8y=s([B.Xv,B.rv],t.P)
B.aex=new A.bC("utis",B.mI,"Why do I keep getting bladder infections?",B.aks,B.b3S,B.b5U,"See your doctor for burning, urgency or cloudy urine. Get care quickly if you have fever, back or side pain, or blood in your urine.",B.b8y,B.bD)
B.b59=s(["Painful sex","Vaginal itching","Dryness down there"],t.s)
B.b2R=s(["vaginal","dryness","painful","sex","intercourse","itching","gsm"],t.s)
B.bfd=s(["Vaginal dryness, itching and discomfort during sex are very common after menopause and, unlike hot flashes, often don't go away on their own.","Vaginal moisturisers (used a few times a week) and lubricants (used during sex) help many women. Low-dose vaginal oestrogen is very effective and considered safe for most women, as very little reaches the rest of the body."],t.s)
B.bnF=s([B.zj,B.Xz],t.P)
B.aeq=new A.bC("vaginal-dryness",B.mI,"What helps with vaginal dryness?",B.b59,B.b2R,B.bfd,"Talk to your doctor: it is a common, treatable problem and worth raising.",B.bnF,B.bD)
B.bbk=s(["Low libido","Not interested in sex"],t.s)
B.bgY=s(["libido","desire","drive","intimacy"],t.s)
B.b2V=s(["Lower desire is common in midlife. Hormone changes, vaginal dryness or discomfort, tiredness, poor sleep, stress, mood, relationships and some medicines can all play a part.","Treating dryness or pain, better sleep, and talking openly with your partner often help."],t.s)
B.b62=s([B.zj,B.rr],t.P)
B.ae4=new A.bC("libido",B.mI,"Why is my sex drive lower?",B.bbk,B.bgY,B.b2V,"If it bothers you, mention it to your doctor; there are options, and they hear about it often.",B.b62,B.bD)
B.b5w=s(["Should I take HRT?","Risks of hormone therapy","MHT","Estrogen therapy"],t.s)
B.b5Z=s(["hrt","hormone","hormones","therapy","mht","estrogen","oestrogen","progesterone","patch"],t.s)
B.bh9=s(["For women within ten years of menopause, Canadian experts (SOGC) and the North American Menopause Society say the benefits of hormone therapy for bothersome symptoms outweigh the risks. It is the most effective treatment for hot flashes and night sweats, and it also protects bone.","Risks depend on your age, health and the type you use. Oestrogen through the skin (patch or gel) has a lower risk of blood clots than pills. If you still have a uterus you also need a progestogen to protect its lining."],t.s)
B.baW=s([B.XH,B.X5,B.Xc],t.P)
B.aec=new A.bC("hrt-safe",B.mJ,"Is hormone therapy (HRT) safe?",B.b5w,B.b5Z,B.bh9,"Whether it is right for you is a decision to make with your doctor, based on your own and your family's health history.",B.baW,B.bD)
B.b8s=s(["Non-hormonal treatment for hot flashes","Alternatives to HRT"],t.s)
B.b4u=s(["non-hormonal","alternative","alternatives","without hormones","gabapentin","fezolinetant"],t.s)
B.aOS=s(["There are several prescription options that are not hormones and can reduce hot flashes, including some antidepressants in low doses, gabapentin, and newer medicines made specifically for hot flashes.","CBT and clinical hypnosis also have good evidence, and they have no side effects."],t.s)
B.b4j=s([B.ze,B.Xr],t.P)
B.aes=new A.bC("non-hormonal",B.mJ,"What can I take if I can't use hormones?",B.b8s,B.b4u,B.aOS,"Your doctor can explain which might suit you.",B.b4j,B.bD)
B.aTe=s(["Compounded hormones","Natural hormones"],t.s)
B.b3Y=s(["bioidentical","compounded","natural","body-identical"],t.s)
B.b5p=s(['"Bioidentical" means hormones with the same structure as the body\'s own. Some approved products in Canada are like this (estradiol patches and gels, micronized progesterone).','Custom-compounded "bioidentical" mixes made by some pharmacies are not tested or regulated the same way, so their strength and safety are less certain. SOGC recommends approved products instead.'],t.s)
B.bqO=s([B.X9],t.P)
B.aeg=new A.bC("bioidentical",B.mJ,"What are bioidentical hormones?",B.aTe,B.b3Y,B.b5p,null,B.bqO,B.bD)
B.bbz=s(["Herbal remedies for menopause","Evening primrose oil","Natural supplements for hot flashes"],t.s)
B.bhb=s(["supplement","supplements","herbal","cohosh","primrose","ginseng","clover","remedies","natural"],t.s)
B.b6R=s(['Many supplements are sold for menopause (black cohosh, red clover, evening primrose, ginseng and others). Good studies show little or no benefit for most, and "natural" doesn\'t always mean safe: black cohosh has been linked to rare liver problems.',"Products vary a lot in what they contain. In Canada, look for an NPN (Natural Product Number) on the label, which means Health Canada has reviewed it."],t.s)
B.b33=s([B.za],t.P)
B.ae9=new A.bC("supplements",B.mJ,"Do supplements like black cohosh work?",B.bbz,B.bhb,B.b6R,"Tell your doctor or pharmacist about any supplement, as some interact with medicines.",B.b33,B.bD)
B.bqN=s(["What should I ask my doctor?","Preparing for an appointment","My doctor doesn't listen"],t.s)
B.b75=s(["appointment","doctor","visit","prepare","questions","find","specialist","clinic","practitioner","gynecologist","gynaecologist"],t.s)
B.bh5=s(["It helps to go prepared: write down your symptoms, how often they happen and how much they affect you, your period dates, medicines and supplements, and your questions.","Bring it up early in the visit, and say clearly what you want help with. The Journal, blood work PDF and Day summary in Daisy can help you remember details.","The Menopause Foundation of Canada has a free guide to taking charge of your care, and a list to help find a menopause-informed practitioner."],t.s)
B.bp5=s([B.zp,B.XC],t.P)
B.aeX=new A.bC("talk-to-doctor",B.rx,"How do I talk to my doctor about menopause?",B.bqN,B.b75,B.bh5,null,B.bp5,B.bD)
B.b70=s(["Breast cancer screening","Cancer screening after 50"],t.s)
B.b7S=s(["mammogram","breast","screening","cancer","pap","colon"],t.s)
B.b2Y=s(["Screening finds some cancers early, when they are easiest to treat. SOGC suggests menopause is a good time to make a plan with your doctor for breast, colon and cervical cancer screening.","Breast screening programs (mammograms) are different in each province and territory, and your own family history or dense breasts can change what is right for you."],t.s)
B.b6E=s([B.zl],t.P)
B.aeR=new A.bC("mammogram",B.rx,"Do I need a mammogram?",B.b70,B.b7S,B.b2Y,"Ask your doctor or your provincial screening program what you are due for. See your doctor any time you notice a breast lump or change.",B.b6E,B.bD)
B.b3_=s(["Is this an emergency?","Should I go to the ER?"],t.s)
B.b2U=s(["emergency","urgent","er","hospital","911","nurse","811"],t.s)
B.b6K=s(["Call 911 for chest pain or pressure, trouble breathing, signs of stroke (face drooping, weak arm, slurred speech), fainting, or very heavy bleeding.","If you are thinking about suicide, call or text 9-8-8 any time.","For other worries, in most provinces you can call 811 to talk to a registered nurse for free, any time of day."],t.s)
